            "review_text": "fleetfoxx\nSydney, Australia111 contributions\n0\n100000 dong for Hu tieu soup\nJan 2018 • Couples\nWe went here as it was recommended in a French blog, and because other recommendations made in this blog were very good. However upon viewing the menu and realising the price (100k), we just got one to share. \nThe Hu Tieu soup was very good, came with lots of herbs but not sure if I’d recommend, as I’m sure you can get just as good soup for less than half the price! \nHowever they were very nice to give us another bowl to share (although there was some confusion amongst the staff at the end of our meal to check whether we had one or two bowls- but no dramas there were no issues). \nWe ended up stopping at a local bbq joint for a second dinner on our way back.\nRead more\nWritten February 2, 2018",
