            "review_title": "Review at Hu Tieu Nam Vang Lien Hua",
            "review_text": "Alan Miller\nSydney, Australia188 contributions\n0\nGood, simple food with very reasonable prices\nNov 2016 • Business\nMy Wife and I are here our first night in Ho Chi Minh City.\n\nAfter a long day traveling and flying, we were looking for a light meal that would not sit too heavy in our stomachs.\n\nWe both ended up ordering the stir-fried beef on vermicelli. Service was quick, friendly and efficient. The waiter showed us how to add the various condiments on the table to and more flavour/heat to the base dish if you do choose.\n\nFood was delicious, the serving was just right, and the staff were very helpful. Prices were most reasonable.\n\nMy wife's parents arrived a few days later to join us on an upcoming tour. We took them here as their first meal in Vietnam. They were very surprised but how good the food was. Especially when the bill was less than 500,000 dhong for 4 people with a drinks.\nRead more\nWritten November 2, 2016",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
