            "review_title": "Review at Hu Tieu Nam Vang Lien Hua",
            "review_text": "Hansai_Dinh\nLos Angeles, California41 contributions\n0\nOverpriced\nFeb 2016 • Friends\nThis place offers a few simple dishes, with so so quality, tiny portion, but overpriced. The noodle is bland, the xiu mai, meat bun, etc (appetizers) are old and tasteless. When you order a bowl of noodle, they bring out a plate of appetizers (4 kind of dim sum) even if you don't order it. It just sit there until you finish your meal, and get cold. The waitress would just take the one you didn't eat, and put it back in the steam container to \"refresh\" it to serve other customers.\n\nThe \"homemade\" yogurt was too sweet. Service was ok, but the owner sits on a kind of platform on some sort of mezzanine and barks orders to the young waiters and waitresses. I would not return.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 8, 2016",
